  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "title": "Question and scope",
      "body": "After a five-minute GC close at or below EMA225 minus three residual standard deviations, how much adverse and favorable excursion occurs from the next complete unadjusted open? The default saved comparison uses ten-bar cooldown and twenty future five-minute bars, a hundred-minute horizon."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "findings",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "The saved yearly table reports both adverse and favorable path extrema rather than choosing an MFE exit. Coverage, valid denominators and uncertainty differ by year. The larger cooldown/horizon grid is a correlated sensitivity, not independent replication or optimized trading evidence."
    },
