    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "methods",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "EMA uses adjusted five-minute closes; sigma is population standard deviation of rolling close-minus-EMA residuals, with pinned readiness and feature availability. Outcomes use raw contract coordinates from the next full five-minute open. MAE and MFE are nonnegative extrema over the whole eligible future path and need not occur in an executable order. Saved approximate 95% ISO-week bootstrap bounds accompany yearly means. Accepted signals include later excluded paths; valid n is the outcome denominator. The twenty-bar horizon must be contiguous, complete and retain contract/adjustment identity."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "Coverage begins partway through 2010 and 2026 is YTD through September 18. Whole-day and adjusted continuous history eligibility is retrospective rather than point-in-time. Missing minutes, partial bars, gaps and roll/adjustment changes exclude paths. No stops, fees, fills, slippage or net profitability were tested; the saved interactive report is not imported into the public page."
    },
